{"name":"Tortuga","hex":"#84816f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tortuga","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An island forming part of Haiti."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tortuga"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tortuga","blocks":[{"text":"Tortuga Island is a West Indian island off the northwest coast of Hispaniola, forming part of Haiti. It constitutes the commune of Île de la Tortue in the Port-de-Paix arrondissement of Haiti's Nord-Ouest department."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Tortuga_Island_NASA.jpg/330px-Tortuga_Island_NASA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tortuga"},{"title":"Tortuga (software)","blocks":[{"text":"Tortuga is an archived software framework for discrete event simulation for the Java programming language last maintained in 2008. A Tortuga simulation can be written either as interacting processes or as scheduled events. A Tortuga simulation can have thousands of entities, and can be part of a larger Java system."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tortuga_(software)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Tortuga17thcentury.jpg/500px-Tortuga17thcentury.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Tortuga17thcentury.jpg/500px-Tortuga17thcentury.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A drawing of Tortuga island from the 17th century.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATortuga17thcentury.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Tortuga_Island_Haiti_2026.jpg/500px-Tortuga_Island_Haiti_2026.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Tortuga_Island_Haiti_2026.jpg/1280